        "original_id": "58d5919c-1b0b-5ff0-99aa-4aa27a1e664c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Kraft, Gene Kranz, Jim Lovell, Jerry Bostick, Ed Fendell, Gene Cernan, John Llewellen, John Aaron, Glynn Lunney, Wally Schirra, Gerry Griffin, Ed Harris\n- Works: Failure Is Not an Option, Apollo 13\n- Organizations: NASA\n- Roles: Flight Director, Mission Control team\n- Programs: Gemini, Apollo, Apollo 11, Apollo 13\n\nFacts:\n- Failure Is Not an Option was produced in 2003.\n- Failure Is Not an Option includes speakers Chris Kraft, Gene Kranz, Jim Lovell, Jerry Bostick, Ed Fendell, Gene Cernan, John Llewellen, John Aaron, Glynn Lunney, Wally Schirra, and Gerry Griffin.\n- Gene Kranz served as a NASA Flight Director during the Gemini and Apollo programs.\n- Chris Kraft was the founding NASA Flight Director, and Gene Kranz was his successor as Flight Director.\n- Gene Kranz served as flight director during Apollo 11, the first lunar landing.\n- Gene Kranz is best known for directing the Mission Control team efforts that helped save the crew of Apollo 13.\n- Apollo 13 later became the subject of a major motion picture of the same name in which Ed Harris portrayed Gene Kranz.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
